        "released_chars": 2592,
        "text": "You told us your July 2026 electric bill was much higher and asked us to confirm whether the meter is broken and to fix the charge. We reviewed your account records and diagnostics and have not found evidence that the meter recorded incorrect energy. At this stage we have not applied any credits or other bill changes. A human reviewer will decide next steps if further inspection or an adjustment is needed.\n\nWhat we reviewed\nWe reviewed the June and July 2026 billing records, the meter register reads taken on 2026-06-30 and 2026-07-31, the declared rate components used to calculate the bills, remote meter diagnostics from 2026-07-29, and the recent monthly usage history contained in your account records.\n\nWhat we found\nThe meter register increased from 41,820 kWh on 2026-06-30 to 42,690 kWh on 2026-07-31, a change of 870 kWh. That register change matches the 870 kWh billed for July 2026. Using the stated energy rate and fixed charge reproduces the billed dollar amounts for June and July. A remote self-test on 2026-07-29 returned a PASS and the diagnostic record shows no tamper or register-fault flags. There are no recorded meter events in the supplied records.\n\nWhy your bill changed\nBased on the records we reviewed, the higher July bill is explained by higher measured consumption for that month: billed kWh increased by 230 kWh compared with June and the meter register change equals the billed amount. We did not find evidence in the supplied diagnostics or event logs that the meter over-recorded usage. However, remote diagnostics have limits and do not absolutely rule out intermittent or installation issues.\n\nWhat happens next\nWe will request additional information to narrow the cause. A human reviewer will be asked to (1) request interval (daily/hourly) usage data for July, (2) request a statement from you about any occupancy or appliance changes in July, and (3) offer a human-reviewed on-site meter inspection if you remain concerned. If new evidence shows a billing error or a confirmed meter fault, a Human Billing Supervisor must review and approve any credit or adjustment before it is applied.\n\nWhat we need from you\nPlease tell us if anything changed at the property in July 2026 (guests, appliance purchases, HVAC use, or other events) and whether you can share any daily usage details or photos of the meter location. If you want an on-site inspection, tell us and we will arrange for a human-reviewed inspection to be scheduled. Do not disconnect or attempt to alter the meter; instead provide the requested information so we can investigate further.",
